MDL101, K15, F1, C5: a UTF-8 byte order mark makes the first line "\ufeff[client]",
which GLib rejects, so mydumper ignores the whole file. The MySQL client
library re-reads the file for the connection (F12) and rejects it too: the BOM
line is an option before any group ("Found option without preceding group"),
so the [client] settings are lost and mydumper, given no connection options on
the command line, cannot connect. (mdl101-bom-cli-connection-drops-masking
shows the masking loss when the command line provides the connection.) The
BOM is also text before '[' on the first line, so the pre-processor does not
reset its state after it (P1, MDL112).
-- scenario --
tool: mydumper
versions: >= v0.19.1-1
args: --defaults-file /work/defaults.cnf --database app
lint: MDL101, MDL112, MDL405
when < v0.19.3-1
# No pre-processor before v0.19.3-1, hence no bracket state leak (MDL112).
lint: MDL101, MDL405
end
expect config-loaded: false
expect exit: nonzero
expect connected: false
expect stderr-contains: Found option without preceding group
-- defaults.cnf.esc --
\xef\xbb\xbf[client]\nhost=mysql\nuser=e2e\npassword=e2e-password\n\n[mydumper]\nthreads=2\n\n[`app`.`users`]\n`email`=random_string\n
